.\" Man page for mapshoot.
.TH MAPSHOOT 1 "2026" "mapshoot 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mapshoot \- render Web Mercator map images from online tile providers with GeoJSON overlays
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mapshoot
.B \-\-bbox
.I west,south,east,north
.B \-\-output
.I map.png
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B mapshoot
.B \-\-center
.I longitude,latitude
.B \-\-radius
.I meters
.B \-\-output
.I map.png
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B mapshoot
.B \-\-geojson
.I file.geojson
.B \-\-output
.I map.png
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mapshoot
renders a PNG map image by fetching raster tiles from an online tile provider
and compositing a GeoJSON overlay on top of them. Tiles are drawn on the CPU
with tiny\-skia; no GPU, display server, or browser is required.
.PP
The output is a single PNG. An area is chosen either from an explicit bounding
box, from a center and radius, or is derived automatically from the extent of
the GeoJSON document. The requested box fills the image; the image height
follows the box aspect ratio in Web Mercator unless it is fixed explicitly.
.PP
Every option accepts either
.B \-\-flag VALUE
or
.BI \-\-flag= VALUE.
Rendering and PNG encoding complete before the destination is written, via a
temporary file that is renamed over the output, so a failed run never leaves a
truncated image behind.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Area
.TP
.BI \-\-bbox " \fIwest,south,east,north\fR"
Bounding box in degrees. Longitudes span \-180..180 and latitudes
\-85.05112878..85.05112878, so the whole world is
.BR \-180,\-85.05112878,180,85.05112878 .
A
.I west
greater than
.I east
crosses the antimeridian.
.TP
.BI \-\-center " \fIlongitude,latitude\fR"
Center of the area; requires
.BR \-\-radius .
Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-bbox .
.TP
.BI \-\-radius " \fImeters\fR"
Radius around
.BR \-\-center ,
from 0 (exclusive) to 1000000. The resulting box wraps in longitude and is
clamped at the Mercator latitude limit.
.TP
.BI \-\-buffer " \fImeters\fR"
Expand the box by this many meters on every side before framing. Default 0.
.TP
.BI \-\-padding " \fImeters\fR"
Synonym for
.BR \-\-buffer .
At most one of the two may be given.
.SS Image
.TP
.BI \-\-width " \fIN\fR"
Image width in pixels, 1..8192. Default 1024.
.TP
.BI \-\-height " \fIN\fR"
Image height in pixels, 1..8192. By default the height follows the box aspect
ratio; when given, the box is fitted inside the resulting frame and centered.
.TP
.BI \-\-aspect\-ratio " \fIW:H\fR"
Fix the frame shape as a width\-to\-height ratio, either
.I W:H
or a plain positive number. One of
.B \-\-width
or
.B \-\-height
is derived from the other if omitted.
.TP
.BI \-\-pixel\-ratio " \fIN\fR"
Integer output scale, 1..4. Default 1. Multiplies the output dimensions;
width times height times the square of this value must not exceed 64 megapixels.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-zoom " \fIN\fR"
Highest tile zoom level, 0..22. Default 19 for
.BR osm ,
20 for
.B here
and
.BR carto .
Tiles are rendered at
.IR ceil(log2(scale / tile_size)) ,
capped at this value.
.TP
.BI \-\-tile\-size " \fIN\fR"
Tile edge length, 256 or 512. Default 256.
.B osm
and
.B carto
accept only 256.
.TP
.BI \-\-concurrency " \fIN\fR"
Parallel tile downloads, 1..32. Default 2 for
.B osm
and 8 for
.B here
and
.BR carto .
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " \fIN\fR"
Total deadline for the tile download phase in milliseconds, 1..300000.
Default 15000.
.SS Basemap
.TP
.BI \-\-basemap " \fIprovider\fR"
One of
.BR here ,
.BR osm ,
.BR carto ,
.BR xyz ,
or
.BR none .
Default
.BR osm ,
which needs no API key.
.B none
draws overlays on a plain #dddddd background and prints a warning.
.TP
.BI \-\-here\-style " \fINAME\fR"
HERE only. Default
.BR explore.day .
See
.B BASEMAP STYLES
below.
.TP
.BI \-\-carto\-style " \fINAME\fR"
CARTO only. Default
.BR voyager .
See
.B BASEMAP STYLES
below.
.TP
.BI \-\-tile\-url " \fIURL\fR"
XYZ only. An HTTP(S) URL template containing the placeholders
.BR {z} ,
.BR {x} ,
and
.BR {y} .
Any credentials belong in this URL.
.TP
.BI \-\-attribution " \fITEXT\fR"
XYZ only and required. Plain printable ASCII, validated to fit the image.
.SS Overlay and output
.TP
.BI \-\-geojson " \fIFILE\fR"
GeoJSON overlay, used with any basemap. Feature, FeatureCollection,
GeometryCollection, Point, LineString, Polygon and their Multi variants are
accepted; null geometries and empty collections are allowed, and polygon rings
must be closed. When neither
.B \-\-bbox
nor
.B \-\-center
is given, the box is derived from the document over the shortest longitude arc
and expanded to include markers and stroke widths.
.TP
.BI \-\-style " \fIFILE\fR"
JSON object with global style fields
.BR color ,
.BR fillColor ,
.BR weight ,
.BR opacity ,
.BR fillOpacity ,
and
.BR radius .
Colors are #RRGGBB, opacities 0..1, and widths and radii are in logical pixels.
Unknown fields are an error.
.TP
.BI \-\-output ", " \-o " \fIFILE\fR"
Required. PNG destination path, or
.B \-
for standard output. Only PNG output is supported, so the path must end in
.BR .png
unless it is
.BR \- .
.SS Cache
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cache
Disable the tile cache for this run.
.TP
.BI \-\-cache\-dir " \fIPATH\fR"
Cache base directory. The default is the per\-user system cache directory; the
version component
.B v1
is always appended.
.TP
.BI \-\-cache\-ttl " \fIDAYS\fR"
Freshness lifetime of cached tiles, 1..3650 days. Default 7.
.TP
.BI \-\-cache\-max\-mb " \fIMB\fR"
Cache size cap in megabytes, 1..102400. Default 512. The cache is trimmed
oldest\-first to 90% of the cap.
.SS General
.TP
.B \-\-help ", " \-h
Print a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH BASEMAP STYLES
.TP
.B HERE
explore.day, explore.night, explore.satellite.day, lite.day, lite.night,
lite.satellite.day, logistics.day, logistics.night, logistics.satellite.day,
satellite.day, topo.day, topo.night, dem.
.TP
.B CARTO
voyager, voyager_nolabels, voyager_labels_under, light_all, light_nolabels,
dark_all, dark_nolabels.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MAPSHOOT_HERE_API_KEY
HERE API key. Takes precedence over
.BR HERE_API_KEY .
.TP
.B MAPSHOOT_CARTO_API_KEY
CARTO API key. Takes precedence over
.BR CARTO_API_KEY .
.TP
.B MAPSHOOT_CACHE_DIR
Cache base directory, overriding the system default. An empty value disables
caching. Ignored when
.B \-\-cache\-dir
is given.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred. With
.BR "\-o \-" ,
a broken pipe (for example
.BR "mapshoot ... | head" )
is treated as success.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/mapshoot/v1
Default tile cache on Linux.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/mapshoot/v1
Fallback tile cache location on Linux when
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
is unset.
.TP
.I ~/Library/Caches/mapshoot/v1
Default tile cache on macOS.
.TP
.I %LOCALAPPDATA%\emapshoot\ev1
Default tile cache on Windows.
.SH EXAMPLES
Render OpenStreetMap with a styled overlay:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
mapshoot \-\-center 13.405,52.52 \-\-radius 1500 \\
  \-\-geojson berlin.geojson \-\-style berlin\-style.json \\
  \-\-output berlin.png
.fi
.RE
.PP
Render a bounding box and write PNG bytes to standard output:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
mapshoot \-\-bbox 13.37,52.50,13.44,52.54 \-o \- > berlin.png
.fi
.RE
.PP
Derive the area from the GeoJSON extent, using per\-feature simplestyle colors:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
mapshoot \-\-geojson simplestyle.geojson \-\-basemap none \-\-width 800 \-o map.png
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
The project README and the library API at
.IR https://github.com/baol/mapshoot .
